<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Yin (206 BC)</h1><p class="st-meta">206 BCE – 205 BCE · capital Zhaoge</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the Eighteen Kingdoms created by Xiang Yu in 206 BCE, held by the Zhao general Sima Ang until he surrendered to Liu Bang a year later.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> divided the empire into eighteen kingdoms in 206 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-ang">Sima Ang</a>, a general of the revived state of Zhao who had captured the Henei region, was made King of Yin, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhaoge">Zhaoge</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, the old <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/shang-dynasty">Shang</a> capital area.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was a military holding with no time to develop institutions of its own. It covered the Henei commandery north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> and served as a buffer between the kingdoms around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> and those of Zhao.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 205 BCE, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> advanced east from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-han-206-bc">Kingdom of Han</a> (206 BC), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-ang">Sima Ang</a> was captured or surrendered, and his realm became the Henei commandery of Han. Sima Ang was later claimed as an ancestor of the Sima family who founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-jin">Western Jin</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 206 BCE – 205 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden=